{
  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "scope": "Actual deletion-receipt target encoding, durable catalog append and exact reclaim effects. Native physical-deletion/path/parent and recovered-lock correspondence remain separate obligations.",
  "properties": {
    "gc_receipt::event": "Resolved encoding contains exactly the supplied canonical name set, no owner/pack/mark/edge/handoff fields, and path_encoding=1. Duplicates are permitted without changing the set meaning.",
    "gc_receipt::{reclaim_one,reclaim_fold,wire_receipts,append_receipts}": "The actual decoded and confirmed operation sequence removes exactly the marked supplied targets from pending deletion and pack indexes; permanent tombstones, owners, edges and consumed handoffs remain unchanged.",
    "gc_receipt::{completed,mark_preserves_completed,receipt_completes_exactly}": "Completed receipts project to deleted minus pending. Marking preserves that projection, while a receipt adds exactly its already-marked targets. This is the logical catalog projection, not a proof of physical absence.",
    "gc_receipt::record": "Composes event construction with actual catalog_append under Writer/Resolver/JSON contracts. Nonempty success adds one confirmed durable frame at the matching cursor/floor, explicitly binds its raw payload/operations to receipt_event through receipt_record, and produces the exact reclaim state. Empty input performs no append. Errors preserve confirmed history, and uncertain write errors keep the log unavailable."
  },
  "runtime_changes": "Native BatchIo::receipt passes the same canonical targets selected from pending deletion directly to the verified record function. It retains before_gc_receipt, the final context check and existing write/sync hooks. It removes redundant canonical-name reinterpretation and a set/JSON round trip after physical deletion. The existing path_encoding=1 format is retained; the target array now follows the supplied snapshot rather than re-sorting via BTreeSet, and its order is not a protocol guarantee. No new file operation/barrier; no performance claim.",
  "boundaries": [
    "The initial log is valid, ready and interpreted; supplied targets are already marked canonical identities. Actual native callers must establish those premises and bind the targets to durable physical absence.",
    "Writer, Resolver, JSON encoding/observation and String key contracts remain explicit. Thin File/Resolver wrappers, original lock/descriptor/context and physical unlink/repair/synchronization conformance are not established by receipt encoding.",
    "An uncertain write can leave an unconfirmed complete durable frame, later admitted by recovery. Keeping confirmed in-memory history unchanged does not assert rollback of physical effects.",
    "Full application roots, concurrent ownership, complete native GC refinement, discovery/retry progress and crashed-writer retirement remain open. No new trusted library primitive or admitted straw body was added.",
    "This extends actual implementation composition; no new production defect is claimed. Two semantic controls deliberately alter the logical reclaim projection rather than a runtime branch."
  ],
